    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Air-sea interaction",
    "problem": "Existing ocean models often neglect the \"current feedback\" on surface wind stress, a crucial energy sink for mesoscale eddies, leading to inaccuracies in simulating air-sea momentum transfer and the overall state of ocean circulation.",
    "method": "This study proposes a method using linear regression between satellite-derived surface stress curl and current vorticity to define a coupling coefficient that quantifies the current-induced wind stress and the resulting sink of oceanic mesoscale eddy energy to the atmosphere.",
    "task": "The task is to use global satellite measurements of surface stress and currents to quantify the linear relationship between them and to determine how the resulting coupling coefficient depends on mean surface wind.",
    "model": [
        "NCEP",
        "ERA"
    ],
